-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ג/7 (16.2.2023): עדכון תוספת שקלית 2016 לעובדי הוראה.
-- The index update of the 2016 shekel supplement from 1.1.2023 for teaching
-- employees in kindergartens, primary and junior-high schools and teacher-
-- training colleges: who is covered, the amounts by Ofek Hadash grade, and
-- when the owners pay.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- Time in this file is counted in salary MONTHS from December 2022
-- (month 0): January 2023 is 1, February 2023 is 2.
`January 2023`  MEANS 1
`February 2023` MEANS 2

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ג/7`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 The letterhead, date, reference number, circular number, addressee (the owners of educational institutions), greeting and subject line; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p13 The sources: the wage agreements of 30.9.2016 (§6ד) and 19.3.2017 and circular תשפ"ב/5 — the 2016 shekel supplement is linked to the consumer price index; the amounts below carry it.
-- akn:hc_1/p14 The circular's purpose: to publish the index update of the 2016 shekel supplement for the period from 1.1.2023; the update itself is ¶19-¶22.

§§ `Indexation`

-- ¶15: the supplement is linked to the December 2022 index (published in
-- January 2023) against the December 2020 index (published in January
-- 2021). The circular prints neither index nor the agreed base amount, so
-- both are inputs; the amounts it prints (¶20-¶22) are data below.
@ref akn:hc_1/p15
GIVEN `amount at the base index` IS A NUMBER @desc the supplement's amount as the agreements set it at the December 2020 index (not printed in this circular)
      `index of December 2022`  IS A NUMBER @desc the consumer price index for December 2022, published in January 2023
      `index of December 2020`  IS A NUMBER @desc the consumer price index for December 2020, published in January 2021
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the indexed amount` `amount at the base index` `index of December 2022` `index of December 2020` IS
    `amount at the base index` TIMES (`index of December 2022` DIVIDED BY `index of December 2020`)

§§ `תחולה`

@desc The stage of education a teaching employee is employed in, as far as this circular asks.
DECLARE `education stage` IS ONE OF
    `kindergarten`
    `primary school`
    `junior high school`
    `teacher-training college`
    `upper division`
    `other stage`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as this circular asks about one.
DECLARE `circular 7 employee` HAS
    `graded in the teaching employees' grading`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by an owner of a supervised institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the employer owns an educational institution supervised by the Ministry of Education
    `stage employed in`                                IS AN `education stage`
    `employed under Ofek Hadash`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed under the terms of the Ofek Hadash reform
    `Ofek Hadash grade`                                IS A NUMBER  @desc the grade (דרגה) the employee is placed in on the Ofek Hadash salary tables; 0 if none
    `position fraction`                                IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position held (1 = a full position)

-- akn:hc_1/p16 The heading "תחולה" (application); no rule.

-- ¶17 defines "עובד הוראה" for the circular: graded in the teaching
-- grading, employed by an owner of a supervised institution, in
-- kindergartens, primary and junior-high schools or teacher-training colleges.
@ref akn:hc_1/p17
GIVEN e IS A `circular 7 employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circular applies to` e IF
        e's `graded in the teaching employees' grading`
    AND e's `employed by an owner of a supervised institution`
    AND `a stage the circular covers` (e's `stage employed in`)

GIVEN s IS AN `education stage`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a stage the circular covers` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `kindergarten` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `primary school` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `junior high school` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `teacher-training college` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ¶18: for the avoidance of doubt, under Ofek Hadash and outside it alike —
-- whether the employee is in the reform plays no part in `the circular applies to`.
@ref akn:hc_1/p18
GIVEN e IS A `circular 7 employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reform status does not affect application` e IF
    `the circular applies to` e EQUALS `the circular applies to` (`the same employee in the other regime` e)

GIVEN x IS A `circular 7 employee`
GIVETH A `circular 7 employee`
DECIDE `the same employee in the other regime` x IS
    `circular 7 employee` WITH
        `graded in the teaching employees' grading`        IS x's `graded in the teaching employees' grading`
        `employed by an owner of a supervised institution` IS x's `employed by an owner of a supervised institution`
        `stage employed in`                                IS x's `stage employed in`
        `employed under Ofek Hadash`                       IS NOT x's `employed under Ofek Hadash`
        `Ofek Hadash grade`                                IS x's `Ofek Hadash grade`
        `position fraction`                                IS x's `position fraction`

§§ `הסכומים מיום 1.1.2023`

@desc One printed amount of the 2016 shekel supplement: the Ofek Hadash grade it is paid at, and the monthly amount for a full position from 1.1.2023.
DECLARE `grade amount row` HAS
    `row grade`              IS A NUMBER
    `full-position amount`   IS A NUMBER

-- ¶19: from 1.1.2023 the amount of the 2016 shekel supplement for a
-- teaching employee in a FULL position is as follows (¶20-¶22).
@ref akn:hc_1/p19
@export The monthly 2016 shekel supplement (תוספת שקלית 2016) for a FULL position that a teaching employee in kindergarten, primary, junior high or a teacher-training college is owed from 1 January 2023 under circular תשפ"ג/7; 0 outside the circular's scope or before January 2023
GIVEN e IS A `circular 7 employee` @desc the employee
      `month` IS A NUMBER @desc the salary month, counted from December 2022 (January 2023 = 1)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `full-position 2016 shekel supplement` e `month` IS
    IF `the circular applies to` e AND `month` AT LEAST `January 2023`
    THEN CONSIDER `the printed rows for` e
         WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN x
         OTHERWISE `the amount for every other teaching employee`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN e IS A `circular 7 employee`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the printed rows for` e IS
    IF e's `employed under Ofek Hadash`
    THEN map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `full-position amount`)
             (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row grade` EQUALS e's `Ofek Hadash grade`) `the amounts by grade from 1.1.2023`)
    ELSE EMPTY

-- ¶20-¶21 as printed: grades 1 to 4.5 on the Ofek Hadash salary tables for
-- academic and non-academic teachers, in shekels a month.
@ref akn:hc_1/p20 akn:hc_1/p21
`the amounts by grade from 1.1.2023` MEANS
    LIST `grade amount row` 1   1173.52,
         `grade amount row` 1.5 1104.83,
         `grade amount row` 2   1036.14,
         `grade amount row` 2.5 952.99,
         `grade amount row` 3   869.86,
         `grade amount row` 3.5 825.34,
         `grade amount row` 4   780.83,
         `grade amount row` 4.5 687.01

-- ¶22: every other teaching employee the circular covers, in Ofek Hadash
-- or not, who is not listed above.
@ref akn:hc_1/p22
`the amount for every other teaching employee` MEANS 593.47

-- ¶23-¶24: the other rules for paying the supplement — among them how a
-- part-time position is paid — are those of circular תשע"ז/3 (linked in
-- ¶24). This circular does not restate them, so the share of the
-- full-position amount an employee receives is an input.
@ref akn:hc_1/p23 akn:hc_1/p24
GIVEN e IS A `circular 7 employee` @desc the employee
      `month` IS A NUMBER @desc the salary month, counted from December 2022 (January 2023 = 1)
      `share under circular תשע"ז/3` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of the full-position amount the rules of circular תשע"ז/3 give this employee (for instance by position fraction); not set by this circular
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `2016 shekel supplement payable` e `month` `share under circular תשע"ז/3` IS
    `full-position 2016 shekel supplement` e `month` TIMES `share under circular תשע"ז/3`

§§ `Payment`

DECLARE `circular 7 action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the updated supplement with January's differences` HAS `amount for January` IS A NUMBER

-- ¶25: paid from January 2023's salary and no later than February 2023's,
-- with retroactive differences for January 2023.
@ref akn:hc_1/p25
GIVEN e IS A `circular 7 employee`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `circular 7 action`
DECIDE `payment of the updated supplement` e IS
    IF `the circular applies to` e
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `pay the updated supplement with January's differences` `paid for January`
               PROVIDED `paid for January` AT LEAST (`full-position 2016 shekel supplement` e `January 2023` TIMES e's `position fraction`)
         WITHIN `February 2023`
         LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ג/7: the updated supplement is paid no later than February 2023's salary, with January's differences"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ¶26: the Ministry reimburses the owners through the relevant hour costs
-- in the payments system.
@ref akn:hc_1/p26
DECLARE `reimbursement channel` IS ONE OF
    `the relevant hour costs in the payments system`

`how the owners are reimbursed` MEANS
    `the relevant hour costs in the payments system`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off, the signatories and the list of copies; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples. The employees are made up; the amounts are the circular's.
GIVEN `in Ofek` IS A BOOLEAN, `grade` IS A NUMBER, `stage` IS AN `education stage`
GIVETH A `circular 7 employee`
DECIDE `an employee` `in Ofek` `grade` `stage` IS
    `circular 7 employee` WITH
        `graded in the teaching employees' grading`        IS TRUE
        `employed by an owner of a supervised institution` IS TRUE
        `stage employed in`                                IS `stage`
        `employed under Ofek Hadash`                       IS `in Ofek`
        `Ofek Hadash grade`                                IS `grade`
        `position fraction`                                IS 1

#ASSERT `full-position 2016 shekel supplement` (`an employee` TRUE 1 `primary school`) `January 2023` EQUALS 1173.52
#ASSERT `full-position 2016 shekel supplement` (`an employee` TRUE 2.5 `kindergarten`) `January 2023` EQUALS 952.99
#ASSERT `full-position 2016 shekel supplement` (`an employee` TRUE 4.5 `junior high school`) `January 2023` EQUALS 687.01
-- Grade 5 is not printed, so it takes the amount for every other employee.
#ASSERT `full-position 2016 shekel supplement` (`an employee` TRUE 5 `primary school`) `January 2023` EQUALS 593.47
-- Outside the reform, the grade plays no part.
#ASSERT `full-position 2016 shekel supplement` (`an employee` FALSE 1 `teacher-training college`) `January 2023` EQUALS 593.47
-- The upper division is outside this circular.
#ASSERT `full-position 2016 shekel supplement` (`an employee` TRUE 1 `upper division`) `January 2023` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `full-position 2016 shekel supplement` (`an employee` TRUE 1 `primary school`) 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the reform status does not affect application` (`an employee` TRUE 3 `kindergarten`)
#ASSERT `2016 shekel supplement payable` (`an employee` TRUE 2 `primary school`) `January 2023` 0.5 EQUALS 518.07
-- Each printed grade has one row and the amounts fall as the grade rises.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN g YIELD count (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row grade` EQUALS g) `the amounts by grade from 1.1.2023`) EQUALS 1)
            (LIST 1, 1.5, 2, 2.5, 3, 3.5, 4, 4.5)
#EVAL `the indexed amount` 1000 110 100

#TRACE `payment of the updated supplement` (`an employee` TRUE 1 `primary school`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the updated supplement with January's differences` 1173.52 AT 2
#TRACE `payment of the updated supplement` (`an employee` TRUE 1 `primary school`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the updated supplement with January's differences` 1173.52 AT 3
